WEBVTT

﻿1
00:00:01.627 --> 00:00:04.671
[tense music]

2
00:00:05.130 --> 00:00:07.090
- Adolf Hitler
and the Nazi party

3
00:00:07.090 --> 00:00:08.967
have dominated the
hearts and minds

4
00:00:08.967 --> 00:00:11.803
of the German people
for over a decade.

5
00:00:11.803 --> 00:00:15.349
But by the summer of
1944. the Soviet Red Army

6
00:00:15.349 --> 00:00:17.643
and the forces of
the Western allies

7
00:00:17.643 --> 00:00:21.146
are tightening their vice
grip on Hitler's Third Reich.

8
00:00:22.356 --> 00:00:25.526
The Nazi's complete
control is about to crack.

9
00:00:27.236 --> 00:00:29.238
- All wars change the world.

10
00:00:29.238 --> 00:00:31.073
but none of them
changed the world

11
00:00:31.073 --> 00:00:32.491
like the Second World War did.

12
00:00:33.325 --> 00:00:36.328
- Japan's on the march.
Germany's on the march.

13
00:00:37.955 --> 00:00:41.333
No one can imagine the nightmare
they're about to unleash.

14
00:00:41.333 --> 00:00:44.336
The most destructive
war in human history.

15
00:00:44.336 --> 00:00:47.130
- Suddenly the world
is turned upside down

16
00:00:47.130 --> 00:00:48.840
and all hell is let loose.

17
00:00:50.884 --> 00:00:53.762
- The West is stunned by
the speed of the advance.

18
00:00:54.972 --> 00:00:58.517
- You get the allies
led by the big three.

19
00:00:58.517 --> 00:01:00.852
Roosevelt. Churchill. Stalin.

20
00:01:00.852 --> 00:01:06.024
men who are dealing with
immensely complicated questions.

21
00:01:06.149 --> 00:01:09.987
- It's the biggest military
operation of human history.

22
00:01:10.153 --> 00:01:11.488
-The Allies have to
come together

23
00:01:11.655 --> 00:01:13.115
not just militarily.

24
00:01:13.115 --> 00:01:14.408
but industrial scale

25
00:01:14.408 --> 00:01:16.577
it's a global perspective.

26
00:01:16.868 --> 00:01:18.537
- They have to fight
in every climate

27
00:01:18.579 --> 00:01:22.040
from the Arctic
to the jungles of the Pacific

28
00:01:22.082 --> 00:01:25.627
to the deserts of Africa
and the depths of the ocean.

29
00:01:25.669 --> 00:01:28.255
♪

30
00:01:28.255 --> 00:01:31.049
- But there was
no certainty of victory.

31
00:01:31.091 --> 00:01:34.636
It was going to be
a horrific bloodbath.

32
00:01:34.678 --> 00:01:36.680
- We see humans
at their absolute worst.

33
00:01:36.722 --> 00:01:39.099
how they treat other
human beings.

34
00:01:39.099 --> 00:01:40.767
And we see them
at their absolute best.

35
00:01:40.809 --> 00:01:43.186
willing to give their lives
that others might live.

36
00:01:43.186 --> 00:01:46.231
- World War II was a struggle
in which there could be

37
00:01:46.273 --> 00:01:49.568
one victor and one vanquished.

38
00:01:49.568 --> 00:01:54.740
♪

39
00:01:54.740 --> 00:01:58.243
[explosion rumbles]

40
00:01:58.243 --> 00:02:00.829
[siren blares]

41
00:02:02.000 --> 00:02:08.074
Support us and become VIP member 
to remove all ads from www.OpenSubtitles.org

42
00:02:11.923 --> 00:02:14.176
- [Reporter] The biggest
story in Western Europe today

43
00:02:14.176 --> 00:02:17.054
is the attempted
assassination of Hitler.

44
00:02:17.054 --> 00:02:19.640
For the second time
since this war began.

45
00:02:19.640 --> 00:02:22.893
an assassin has almost
succeeded in killing the Führer

46
00:02:22.893 --> 00:02:25.520
and perhaps changing
the course of history.

47
00:02:26.521 --> 00:02:29.107
[tense music]

48
00:02:31.777 --> 00:02:34.529
- [Tom] July 20th. 1944.

49
00:02:35.656 --> 00:02:37.866
A bomb hidden in a
briefcase explodes

50
00:02:37.866 --> 00:02:41.536
at the Wolf's Lair. Adolf
Hitler's military headquarters.

51
00:02:44.956 --> 00:02:47.292
It was the opening move
in an elaborate plan

52
00:02:47.292 --> 00:02:49.961
to kill the Nazi leader and
overthrow his government.

53
00:02:52.881 --> 00:02:57.552
Hitler is wounded but
survives. and the plot fails.

54
00:02:58.679 --> 00:03:03.475
[Adolf Hitler speaking German]

55
00:03:16.780 --> 00:03:20.033
- Surviving the July 20th
bombing convinces Hitler

56
00:03:20.033 --> 00:03:24.287
beyond a shadow of a doubt that
he has been chosen by heaven

57
00:03:24.287 --> 00:03:28.041
or by providence to
lead the German people.

58
00:03:31.253 --> 00:03:33.839
- He's on all sorts
of medications.

59
00:03:33.839 --> 00:03:37.426
He's under more pressure than
most human beings can imagine.

60
00:03:39.553 --> 00:03:42.597
- He becomes even more paranoid
than he already has been.

61
00:03:42.597 --> 00:03:44.933
He is micromanaging even more.

62
00:03:46.017 --> 00:03:48.603
Nazis take over
armaments production.

63
00:03:48.603 --> 00:03:51.815
[crowd chatter indistinctly]

64
00:03:51.815 --> 00:03:54.443
- [Tom] Hitler and the
Nazis mobilize even more men

65
00:03:54.443 --> 00:03:57.195
and tighten their grip on
Germany and its people.

66
00:04:00.449 --> 00:04:02.492
- There is no difference anymore

67
00:04:02.492 --> 00:04:04.744
between the fate of the
public and the German people

68
00:04:04.744 --> 00:04:07.622
and the fate of the Nazi state.

69
00:04:08.957 --> 00:04:12.961
The thing is. the German
public is not too happy

70
00:04:12.961 --> 00:04:15.213
about how the war goes on.

71
00:04:15.213 --> 00:04:18.048
They are aware that
Germany may lose the war.

72
00:04:18.048 --> 00:04:21.887
but they think the only
person who can bring this

73
00:04:21.887 --> 00:04:23.889
to a close is Hitler himself.

74
00:04:28.059 --> 00:04:29.436
- [Tom] As summer turns to fall.

75
00:04:29.436 --> 00:04:32.481
Germany's strategic
situation deteriorates.

76
00:04:33.648 --> 00:04:35.609
and every German is aware

77
00:04:35.609 --> 00:04:39.029
that the allies demand
unconditional surrender.

78
00:04:40.530 --> 00:04:42.866
- [James] Hitler knows that
that's an impossibility.

79
00:04:43.658 --> 00:04:45.076
Surrender means

80
00:04:45.076 --> 00:04:48.205
humiliation. being betrayed.
ultimately executed.

81
00:04:48.789 --> 00:04:51.249
- [Robert] Hitler also knows
something about warfare.

82
00:04:51.249 --> 00:04:53.585
A passive defense never works.

83
00:04:54.461 --> 00:04:56.505
You have to show
your adversaries

84
00:04:56.505 --> 00:04:58.131
that you're still dangerous.

85
00:04:59.966 --> 00:05:01.843
Hitler quotes
Frederick the Great

86
00:05:01.843 --> 00:05:04.930
who was in a similar
war in the 18th century.

87
00:05:04.930 --> 00:05:07.641
Frederick famously said.
"We're gonna fight this war

88
00:05:07.641 --> 00:05:10.352
till one of our goddamn
enemies gets tired."

89
00:05:12.145 --> 00:05:15.357
- Hitler wants to come
up with some Hail Mary.

90
00:05:15.357 --> 00:05:17.526
He wants to come
up with some plan

91
00:05:17.526 --> 00:05:19.152
that will bring advantage back

92
00:05:19.152 --> 00:05:21.863
to a heavily
disadvantaged situation.

93
00:05:27.452 --> 00:05:30.163
- [Tom] In September.
Hitler summons his generals

94
00:05:30.163 --> 00:05:31.623
to the Wolf's Lair.

95
00:05:33.083 --> 00:05:35.669
He outlines a plan that
will return his troops

96
00:05:35.669 --> 00:05:39.881
to the scene of his greatest
triumph. the Ardennes.

97
00:05:43.927 --> 00:05:45.887
- [Robert] The Ardennes
Offensive of 1944

98
00:05:45.887 --> 00:05:48.056
is going to involve multiple
German armies

99
00:05:48.056 --> 00:05:50.267
across 100 miles of front.

100
00:05:50.267 --> 00:05:53.353
They're going to crash through
what they have identified

101
00:05:53.353 --> 00:05:56.690
as a weakly held portion
of the American line.

102
00:05:56.690 --> 00:05:59.150
They're going to drive
through the Ardennes Forest.

103
00:05:59.150 --> 00:06:01.361
scene of the great
victory of 1940.

104
00:06:01.361 --> 00:06:04.197
and if all goes well.
cross the Meuse River.

105
00:06:04.197 --> 00:06:06.616
and from there.
make it to Antwerp.

106
00:06:06.616 --> 00:06:08.451
Antwerp is the major supply port

107
00:06:08.451 --> 00:06:11.162
for the entire allied
force in Europe.

108
00:06:11.162 --> 00:06:14.499
If the Germans take Antwerp.
it will be a catastrophe

109
00:06:14.499 --> 00:06:16.376
of unimaginable proportions.

110
00:06:18.378 --> 00:06:21.631
- Hitler sees this as a way
to divide the coalition.

111
00:06:21.631 --> 00:06:23.258
demoralize the coalition.

112
00:06:23.258 --> 00:06:24.843
and force the coalition

113
00:06:24.843 --> 00:06:26.595
to make separate
peaces with him.

114
00:06:27.971 --> 00:06:30.265
- [Tom] But Hitler will have
to strip whole divisions

115
00:06:30.265 --> 00:06:34.686
from his Eastern front to
execute his gambit in the West.

116
00:06:39.232 --> 00:06:41.568
- [Robert] Not all of Hitler's
generals are on board.

117
00:06:41.568 --> 00:06:43.278
They just don't believe

118
00:06:43.278 --> 00:06:45.530
that given their
current force levels

119
00:06:45.530 --> 00:06:48.742
that they can blast across
the West European continent

120
00:06:48.742 --> 00:06:51.119
and take the major
city of Antwerp.

121
00:06:52.537 --> 00:06:56.583
Field Marshall Gerd von
Rundstedt says "Antwerp. my god.

122
00:06:56.583 --> 00:06:58.001
if we even get to the Meuse
River

123
00:06:58.001 --> 00:06:59.336
...that's less than halfway....

124
00:06:59.461 --> 00:07:01.546
we should get down on
our knees and thank God."

125
00:07:02.922 --> 00:07:05.008
- [Geoffrey] But Hitler. by this
stage of the war.

126
00:07:05.008 --> 00:07:07.802
he doesn't really trust
very many of his generals.

127
00:07:07.802 --> 00:07:10.639
and he does have
this belief in luck.

128
00:07:10.639 --> 00:07:13.433
He's gotten lucky at various
points throughout this war.

129
00:07:13.433 --> 00:07:15.352
and he might be lucky
again this time.

130
00:07:15.352 --> 00:07:17.312
So he decides to roll the dice.

131
00:07:18.396 --> 00:07:19.898
- [Martin] Hitler will even
eventually say that.

132
00:07:19.898 --> 00:07:22.692
"If this doesn't end well.
I'd see no other path

133
00:07:22.692 --> 00:07:25.153
toward reaching a
favorable conclusion."

134
00:07:26.279 --> 00:07:28.406
The fate of Germany really
hangs in the balance.

135
00:07:30.950 --> 00:07:33.411
[tense music]

136
00:07:41.002 --> 00:07:43.546
- [Robert] December 16th.
it's a snowy morning

137
00:07:43.546 --> 00:07:45.674
in the Ardennes for the allies.

138
00:07:46.966 --> 00:07:48.510
It's overcast.

139
00:07:48.510 --> 00:07:50.345
it's freezing cold.

140
00:07:51.888 --> 00:07:54.683
- The weather was
awful for everybody.

141
00:07:54.683 --> 00:07:56.309
but it gave the
Germans advantage

142
00:07:56.309 --> 00:07:59.562
because the allied aircraft
are mostly grounded.

143
00:07:59.562 --> 00:08:02.482
and that's the perfect
environment for the Germans

144
00:08:02.482 --> 00:08:05.610
to launch this bold offensive.

145
00:08:07.445 --> 00:08:10.448
- Suddenly at 5:30. it seems
that hell has opened up.

146
00:08:10.448 --> 00:08:13.368
[artillery bangs]

147
00:08:15.036 --> 00:08:16.871
Every artillery piece
the Germans own.

148
00:08:16.871 --> 00:08:18.957
heavy artillery.
light artillery.

149
00:08:18.957 --> 00:08:22.001
rocket artillery. the famous
Screaming Mimi's mortars.

150
00:08:23.795 --> 00:08:27.966
The American position in the
Ardennes simply gets shredded.

151
00:08:27.966 --> 00:08:30.552
[bomb booms]

152
00:08:32.761 --> 00:08:34.681
- [Paul] Trees are thrown
through the air

153
00:08:34.681 --> 00:08:37.642
with this just
shell after shell.

154
00:08:37.642 --> 00:08:40.145
[bomb booms]

155
00:08:41.855 --> 00:08:43.898
- [Martin] Allied forces.
they're caught off guard.

156
00:08:43.898 --> 00:08:46.151
They are overwhelmed.

157
00:08:46.151 --> 00:08:48.069
They certainly didn't
expect the Germans capable

158
00:08:48.069 --> 00:08:52.323
of launching something as big
as the Ardennes Offensive.

159
00:08:52.323 --> 00:08:54.075
[guns bang]

160
00:08:54.075 --> 00:08:56.536
- Suddenly there's a couple of
hundred thousand German infantry

161
00:08:56.536 --> 00:09:00.123
with 600 German Panzers
along 100-mile front.

162
00:09:00.123 --> 00:09:02.375
[guns bang]

163
00:09:06.921 --> 00:09:08.089
- [Tom] One of the
four divisions

164
00:09:08.214 --> 00:09:10.383
holding the allied
line in the Ardennes

165
00:09:10.383 --> 00:09:13.428
is the newly arrived
American 106th.

166
00:09:15.555 --> 00:09:18.016
- [Paul] The 106th Division who
are just in the wrong place

167
00:09:18.016 --> 00:09:20.435
at the wrong time who have
columns of German armor

168
00:09:20.435 --> 00:09:21.936
coming at them
from all directions

169
00:09:21.936 --> 00:09:24.481
are just overwhelmed by this.

170
00:09:24.481 --> 00:09:29.444
And within a matter of hours.
7.000 men are captured.

171
00:09:31.321 --> 00:09:32.530
- [Geoffrey] It's the biggest

172
00:09:32.655 --> 00:09:34.824
mass American
surrender since Bataan.

173
00:09:37.994 --> 00:09:40.163
- [Dr. Lieb] At this point of
time. the German troops

174
00:09:40.163 --> 00:09:41.873
are in a state of euphoria.

175
00:09:43.041 --> 00:09:45.960
For weeks or months
or even years.

176
00:09:45.960 --> 00:09:48.129
they had only known retreat.

177
00:09:48.129 --> 00:09:50.298
and now for the first
and for a long time.

178
00:09:50.298 --> 00:09:52.050
they are on the offense again.

179
00:09:54.511 --> 00:09:56.179
- [Martin] German troops are
partly motivated

180
00:09:56.179 --> 00:09:58.890
because they're being
told. "Take no prisoners.

181
00:09:58.890 --> 00:10:00.308
This is your chance.

182
00:10:00.308 --> 00:10:02.227
Now you get revenge
against the Allies."

183
00:10:02.894 --> 00:10:06.564
The result is that there is
literally a trail of massacres

184
00:10:08.483 --> 00:10:11.402
that will lead eventually
to the most notorious

185
00:10:11.402 --> 00:10:12.779
of about a dozen massacres.

186
00:10:12.779 --> 00:10:14.239
and that's the one
that takes place

187
00:10:14.239 --> 00:10:16.658
in the afternoon
of December 17th

188
00:10:16.658 --> 00:10:18.743
just outside the
city of Malmedy.

189
00:10:20.703 --> 00:10:23.164
[tense music]

190
00:10:24.833 --> 00:10:26.876
- [Robert] The first SS Panzer
division.

191
00:10:26.876 --> 00:10:28.336
they've worked their way forward

192
00:10:28.461 --> 00:10:31.256
under their battle group
commander Joachim Peiper.

193
00:10:32.924 --> 00:10:34.676
Peiper's built for speed.

194
00:10:34.676 --> 00:10:37.720
He's been told to get ahead
as fast as you possibly can

195
00:10:37.720 --> 00:10:41.015
towards the Meuse. cross
the river. get to Antwerp.

196
00:10:41.015 --> 00:10:42.350
[cannon booms]

197
00:10:42.350 --> 00:10:43.810
And he's just
overrun a couple of

198
00:10:43.810 --> 00:10:46.104
rear echelon US detachments.

199
00:10:46.104 --> 00:10:48.523
supply depots.
administrative troops.

200
00:10:49.816 --> 00:10:51.359
- There's a brief firefight.

201
00:10:51.359 --> 00:10:54.028
The Americans then
surrender. about 120 of them.

202
00:10:54.028 --> 00:10:56.614
They move them off
the road into a field.

203
00:11:00.160 --> 00:11:03.204
And the result is
that 84 Americans.

204
00:11:03.204 --> 00:11:06.457
they are murdered after having
surrendered their weapons.

205
00:11:10.753 --> 00:11:12.881
- This is one of the
largest war crimes

206
00:11:12.881 --> 00:11:14.883
against US soldiers
during World War II.

207
00:11:14.883 --> 00:11:17.177
and it shows the
ruthlessness which this war

208
00:11:17.177 --> 00:11:18.636
has achieved at this point.

209
00:11:19.679 --> 00:11:22.265
[tense music]

210
00:11:24.017 --> 00:11:25.643
- [Tom] Some German
units advance

211
00:11:25.643 --> 00:11:28.313
as much as 20 miles
on the first day.

212
00:11:29.772 --> 00:11:31.900
The initial success of
the Ardennes Offensive

213
00:11:31.900 --> 00:11:36.070
confirms Hitler's sense
of divine destiny.

214
00:11:36.070 --> 00:11:38.907
- [Dr. Lieb] In Hitler's mind.
he thinks. "Again. I was right.

215
00:11:38.907 --> 00:11:41.201
I took the decision to
launch this offensive

216
00:11:41.201 --> 00:11:43.077
against the advice
of my generals.

217
00:11:43.077 --> 00:11:47.081
against the advice of my
experts. but I was right."

218
00:11:47.081 --> 00:11:50.084
[cannon booms]

219
00:11:50.084 --> 00:11:53.087
So in the first couple of days
of the Ardennes Offensive.

220
00:11:55.173 --> 00:11:56.674
it seems for the Germans

221
00:11:56.674 --> 00:11:58.927
that they have regained
the initiative.

222
00:11:58.927 --> 00:12:01.304
[rockets zoom]

223
00:12:04.390 --> 00:12:05.892
[tense music]

224
00:12:09.354 --> 00:12:10.521
- [Tom] The Wehrmacht's
attack stretches

225
00:12:10.521 --> 00:12:12.190
from Belgium to Luxembourg.

226
00:12:12.607 --> 00:12:15.401
but the initial reports
from the front are sketchy.

227
00:12:19.530 --> 00:12:22.533
How to respond to the German
assault is the responsibility

228
00:12:22.533 --> 00:12:24.911
of one man.

229
00:12:24.911 --> 00:12:27.080
General Dwight Eisenhower.

230
00:12:27.080 --> 00:12:28.831
the Supreme Allied Commander.

231
00:12:30.750 --> 00:12:31.918
- So Eisenhower
has to determine

232
00:12:31.918 --> 00:12:33.378
whether or not this
is a feint. right?

233
00:12:33.378 --> 00:12:35.713
Are the Germans trying to
essentially pull his resources

234
00:12:35.713 --> 00:12:37.590
in the wrong direction?

235
00:12:37.715 --> 00:12:39.759
Or is this a proper offensive?

236
00:12:39.759 --> 00:12:41.511
Does he actually
have to respond?

237
00:12:43.596 --> 00:12:46.182
- Eisenhower immediately
defines the threat.

238
00:12:48.768 --> 00:12:51.646
And he says. "This is
more than a German feint.

239
00:12:51.646 --> 00:12:53.106
This is a major effort."

240
00:12:54.274 --> 00:12:57.568
- And he thinks. let's
not see this disaster

241
00:12:57.568 --> 00:12:59.487
as anything but an opportunity.

242
00:12:59.487 --> 00:13:01.447
The Germans wanna
fight out in the open.

243
00:13:03.241 --> 00:13:04.367
let's take it to them.

244
00:13:06.995 --> 00:13:08.663
- [Geoffrey] Yeah. the Germans
are advancing.

245
00:13:08.663 --> 00:13:11.624
Yeah. the Germans have driven
a deep bulge into my lines.

246
00:13:11.624 --> 00:13:13.835
but that offers me
this big German salient

247
00:13:13.835 --> 00:13:15.878
that I can attack
from the shoulders.

248
00:13:15.878 --> 00:13:18.715
- That's why we refer to this
as the Battle of the Bulge.

249
00:13:20.174 --> 00:13:23.803
- [Tom] The Germans advance
across a 60-mile front.

250
00:13:23.803 --> 00:13:26.931
but are held up by the
US 28th Infantry Division

251
00:13:26.931 --> 00:13:29.267
at the Belgian town of Bastogne.

252
00:13:30.476 --> 00:13:33.563
- [Robert] Both sides know that
Bastogne is the key.

253
00:13:33.563 --> 00:13:36.899
If the Germans seize it. they
can control the road network

254
00:13:36.899 --> 00:13:39.027
and motor all the
way to the West.

255
00:13:39.027 --> 00:13:41.112
perhaps even reach Antwerp.

256
00:13:41.946 --> 00:13:43.406
But if the Americans hold it.

257
00:13:43.406 --> 00:13:45.575
the Germans are stuck
in their tracks.

258
00:13:48.202 --> 00:13:49.412
- [Col. Douds] So it's a race.

259
00:13:49.412 --> 00:13:51.456
it's a race for the Germans
to take it.

260
00:13:51.456 --> 00:13:54.167
It's a race for the Americans
to try and resupply it

261
00:13:54.167 --> 00:13:55.585
before it's lost.

262
00:13:56.627 --> 00:13:58.755
So all of a sudden.
Bastogne becomes

263
00:13:58.755 --> 00:14:00.506
this key road intersection.

264
00:14:00.506 --> 00:14:03.968
not unlike Gettysburg or
Waterloo or Thermopylae.

265
00:14:03.968 --> 00:14:05.303
It is everything.

266
00:14:07.513 --> 00:14:10.892
- [Tom] As the Germans
attempt to surround Bastogne.

267
00:14:10.892 --> 00:14:14.270
Eisenhower calls on the
101st Airborne Division.

268
00:14:15.480 --> 00:14:16.773
the Screaming Eagles.

269
00:14:19.192 --> 00:14:20.943
- [Col. Douds] Their big
contribution so far is

270
00:14:20.943 --> 00:14:24.280
when they get dropped behind
enemy lines before D-Day.

271
00:14:24.280 --> 00:14:26.824
[planes whir]

272
00:14:28.242 --> 00:14:31.704
They've basically been in the
game since June 5th of '44.

273
00:14:33.039 --> 00:14:35.792
- [Robert] To say that the 101s
is unprepared for this fight

274
00:14:35.792 --> 00:14:38.628
is to understate the
matter considerably.

275
00:14:38.628 --> 00:14:40.630
- [Col. Douds] They would
usually jump into war zones

276
00:14:40.630 --> 00:14:42.215
carrying what they can carry.

277
00:14:42.215 --> 00:14:46.719
which inherently means they
don't have a lot of armor.

278
00:14:46.719 --> 00:14:48.596
they don't have any artillery.

279
00:14:48.596 --> 00:14:50.932
- [Robert] They don't have the
winter gear. that equipment

280
00:14:50.932 --> 00:14:53.559
that would allow you
to fight a tough battle

281
00:14:53.559 --> 00:14:54.977
in the middle of December.

282
00:14:54.977 --> 00:14:56.896
It's a come-as-you-are war.

283
00:14:58.231 --> 00:14:59.690
- [Col. Douds] It tells you the
degree

284
00:14:59.690 --> 00:15:01.442
to which this is a crisis.

285
00:15:01.442 --> 00:15:04.362
that in the midst of this
crisis. Eisenhower turns around

286
00:15:04.362 --> 00:15:06.280
and looks and says.
"I'll take them."

287
00:15:08.783 --> 00:15:10.284
Because the one thing they are

288
00:15:10.284 --> 00:15:12.578
is they are a hardened
group of elites.

289
00:15:12.578 --> 00:15:14.664
and they will go in
there and do the job

290
00:15:14.664 --> 00:15:17.083
despite all the
limitations they face.

291
00:15:17.875 --> 00:15:20.503
[tense music]

292
00:15:22.296 --> 00:15:24.382
- [Tom] December 18th.

293
00:15:24.841 --> 00:15:27.510
The 101st is trucked
into Bastogne

294
00:15:27.510 --> 00:15:29.720
to relieve the
battered 28th Division.

295
00:15:32.723 --> 00:15:34.851
The defense of this
Belgian town is the key

296
00:15:34.851 --> 00:15:36.853
to the allied effort
against Adolf Hitler

297
00:15:36.853 --> 00:15:37.937
on the Western front.

298
00:15:39.480 --> 00:15:42.692
And the key to the defense
of this town is in the hands

299
00:15:42.692 --> 00:15:44.694
of the men of the
101st Airborne.

300
00:15:45.653 --> 00:15:48.281
[tense music]

301
00:15:50.449 --> 00:15:51.534
- [Col. Douds] For the Germans.

302
00:15:51.534 --> 00:15:53.035
this whole thing has to
happen fast.

303
00:15:53.035 --> 00:15:54.245
Every day they're standing
in front of Bastogne

304
00:15:54.245 --> 00:15:56.455
is time they don't have.

305
00:15:56.455 --> 00:15:57.957
time where the weather
could clear up.

306
00:15:57.957 --> 00:16:00.209
time where the rest
of the allied armies

307
00:16:00.209 --> 00:16:02.920
are starting to get
reinforcements in there.

308
00:16:02.920 --> 00:16:04.755
- And so the Germans
are determined

309
00:16:04.755 --> 00:16:07.967
to throw everything at Bastogne
that they possibly have.

310
00:16:07.967 --> 00:16:10.636
[cannons boom]

311
00:16:12.847 --> 00:16:15.975
There's an artillery
bombardment.

312
00:16:15.975 --> 00:16:17.810
They're attacking
from all sides.

313
00:16:17.810 --> 00:16:19.896
They're trying to push
the Americans out.

314
00:16:22.773 --> 00:16:24.108
- [Robert] For the 101st
Airborne.

315
00:16:24.108 --> 00:16:25.234
the fighting around Bastogne

316
00:16:25.234 --> 00:16:27.153
is as tough as any in the war.

317
00:16:27.153 --> 00:16:29.238
[gun bangs]

318
00:16:29.238 --> 00:16:31.824
It's out in the open.
it's bitterly cold.

319
00:16:31.824 --> 00:16:33.284
there's snow on the ground.

320
00:16:33.284 --> 00:16:34.994
- [Col. Douds] They're short on
food.

321
00:16:34.994 --> 00:16:38.122
and yet with almost just
small arms. bazookas.

322
00:16:38.122 --> 00:16:41.125
and machine guns. they're
able to put up enough bluster

323
00:16:41.125 --> 00:16:44.212
and defense that they're
able to hold the line.

324
00:16:45.796 --> 00:16:48.257
[tense music]

325
00:16:53.596 --> 00:16:57.058
- [Tom] To reinforce
the 101st in Bastogne.

326
00:16:57.058 --> 00:16:59.894
Eisenhower turns to his
most aggressive commander.

327
00:17:01.270 --> 00:17:03.606
General George Patton
and the Third Army.

328
00:17:05.398 --> 00:17:07.609
- [Michel] Patton. you know.
promises him three divisions

329
00:17:07.609 --> 00:17:09.737
in two days for Bastogne.
which is something

330
00:17:09.737 --> 00:17:12.198
only George S.
Patton would promise.

331
00:17:13.156 --> 00:17:14.325
- [Paul] Promising three
divisions.

332
00:17:14.450 --> 00:17:17.578
And you know. that's 40.000+ men

333
00:17:17.578 --> 00:17:19.829
ready at 48 hours.

334
00:17:21.707 --> 00:17:23.626
- [Michel] Patton had already
planned

335
00:17:23.626 --> 00:17:25.044
for precisely this contingency

336
00:17:25.044 --> 00:17:26.671
and was ready to take the lead

337
00:17:26.671 --> 00:17:28.256
once he was given the operation.

338
00:17:30.716 --> 00:17:32.760
- [Tom] But until the
Third Army arrives.

339
00:17:32.760 --> 00:17:35.721
the Screaming Eagles are
virtually on their own.

340
00:17:38.099 --> 00:17:40.393
- [Martin] The Germans encircle
the city.

341
00:17:40.393 --> 00:17:43.271
and that encirclement
will be headline news

342
00:17:43.271 --> 00:17:44.647
back in the United States.

343
00:17:45.898 --> 00:17:49.026
There was this critical
thought that we might lose

344
00:17:49.026 --> 00:17:52.822
the entire 101st Airborne
Division to the enemy.

345
00:17:54.115 --> 00:17:56.909
- [Alexandra] It looks as if the
Germans are really in control

346
00:17:56.909 --> 00:18:00.288
and they send a message
to the 101st Airborne.

347
00:18:02.164 --> 00:18:04.750
They say. "You've
got to surrender."

348
00:18:07.253 --> 00:18:08.462
- [Col. Douds] They're gonna
give it to the

349
00:18:08.462 --> 00:18:09.922
acting division commander.

350
00:18:09.922 --> 00:18:12.008
Brigadier General Anthony
McAuliffe.

351
00:18:12.008 --> 00:18:13.718
McAuliffe will read the thing

352
00:18:13.718 --> 00:18:16.012
and he'll send back a one-word
reply

353
00:18:16.012 --> 00:18:17.430
and it says. "Nuts!"

354
00:18:20.016 --> 00:18:21.809
Now. you gotta imagine.
you know. some savvy

355
00:18:21.809 --> 00:18:23.227
Airborne officer

356
00:18:23.227 --> 00:18:24.937
gets to go give this to
the German delegation.

357
00:18:24.937 --> 00:18:26.522
Of course. they read
"Nuts" and they're like.

358
00:18:26.522 --> 00:18:28.482
"We don't understand
the colloquialism."

359
00:18:29.609 --> 00:18:31.110
And so he gets to stand
there and he says.

360
00:18:31.110 --> 00:18:32.612
"It's the same as go to hell."

361
00:18:34.488 --> 00:18:37.533
And in a sense. the whole
unit kind of reaches out

362
00:18:37.533 --> 00:18:39.952
and they hit the collective
I believe button.

363
00:18:41.579 --> 00:18:44.081
which is not so much that
they can hold out forever.

364
00:18:44.081 --> 00:18:47.001
but Patton's coming.

365
00:18:47.001 --> 00:18:48.294
They're all coming.

366
00:18:48.419 --> 00:18:50.630
All we have to do is
hold out a little longer.

367
00:18:55.384 --> 00:18:56.510
[tense music]

368
00:18:56.510 --> 00:18:57.511
[cannon booms]

369
00:19:01.599 --> 00:19:03.976
- [Tom] In Bastogne. the men
of the 101st Division

370
00:19:03.976 --> 00:19:06.228
had been under siege
for almost a week.

371
00:19:08.314 --> 00:19:12.068
But on December 26th.
Patton's Third Army

372
00:19:12.068 --> 00:19:13.486
reaches the outskirts.

373
00:19:15.488 --> 00:19:17.740
- [Martin] Famously. it was the
4th Armored Division

374
00:19:17.740 --> 00:19:19.867
that has given the
task of fighting up

375
00:19:19.867 --> 00:19:23.245
a narrow road corridor
toward Bastogne.

376
00:19:23.245 --> 00:19:25.831
[tense music]

377
00:19:30.961 --> 00:19:34.298
And on the day after
Christmas. on December 26th.

378
00:19:34.298 --> 00:19:37.760
elements of C Company of
the 37th Tank Battalion

379
00:19:37.760 --> 00:19:39.762
pull up to the
Bastogne perimeter.

380
00:19:39.762 --> 00:19:43.265
[cannon booms]

381
00:19:43.265 --> 00:19:46.060
- [Col. Douds] The allies break
the German lines.

382
00:19:46.060 --> 00:19:48.896
and now supplies will
be able to flow in.

383
00:19:48.896 --> 00:19:50.523
And so for the Germans.

384
00:19:50.523 --> 00:19:53.609
the Ardennes Offensive
breaks over Bastogne.

385
00:19:53.609 --> 00:19:56.737
[cannon booms]

386
00:19:56.737 --> 00:19:58.823
- [Tom] Even though
Bastogne is relieved.

387
00:19:58.823 --> 00:20:01.867
fighting continues across
the front for weeks.

388
00:20:03.160 --> 00:20:05.746
The United States Army
suffers more casualties

389
00:20:05.746 --> 00:20:07.331
in the Battle of the Bulge

390
00:20:07.331 --> 00:20:09.625
than in any other
battle in its history.

391
00:20:11.711 --> 00:20:15.965
But ultimately Hitler's
Ardennes Offensive is a failure.

392
00:20:17.133 --> 00:20:18.426
- [Robert] For Hitler.

393
00:20:18.426 --> 00:20:19.552
the catastrophe of the Ardennes
is that

394
00:20:19.552 --> 00:20:21.470
it was the last
round in the chamber.

395
00:20:21.762 --> 00:20:23.347
The Germans really poured

396
00:20:23.347 --> 00:20:25.891
their entire armored
reserve into it.

397
00:20:25.891 --> 00:20:27.351
They could have
used those troops

398
00:20:27.351 --> 00:20:29.603
perhaps to defend more robustly

399
00:20:29.603 --> 00:20:31.814
in the east and
west simultaneously.

400
00:20:31.814 --> 00:20:33.733
but they threw them
all away on a gamble

401
00:20:33.733 --> 00:20:35.067
and a gamble that failed.

402
00:20:35.943 --> 00:20:38.487
[somber music]

403
00:20:42.867 --> 00:20:45.536
- [Tom] As the Allies
stop Hitler in the West.

404
00:20:45.536 --> 00:20:48.914
the Soviets launch a massive
offensive in the East.

405
00:20:52.710 --> 00:20:55.087
- The Red Army is a
force of millions.

406
00:20:55.087 --> 00:20:58.591
which has begun its advance
everywhere from Finland

407
00:20:58.591 --> 00:21:00.217
and the Baltics in the north.

408
00:21:00.217 --> 00:21:03.053
all the way down
to the Black Sea in the south.

409
00:21:06.682 --> 00:21:09.727
- The Soviet forces had
advanced incredible speed.

410
00:21:09.727 --> 00:21:11.604
incredible hard fighting.

411
00:21:11.604 --> 00:21:16.025
and Stalin had stopped them
between October and December

412
00:21:16.025 --> 00:21:18.611
for a very clear
strategic purpose.

413
00:21:18.611 --> 00:21:22.865
to prepare a massive.
massive buildup of armor.

414
00:21:24.283 --> 00:21:26.827
- [Sean] So by January '45.

415
00:21:26.827 --> 00:21:28.704
they are ready to go on
the offensive.

416
00:21:28.704 --> 00:21:31.123
[bomb booms]

417
00:21:33.751 --> 00:21:37.755
- [Tom] Within weeks. Soviet
forces cross into Germany.

418
00:21:37.755 --> 00:21:40.883
The Red Army has breached
the border of the Fatherland.

419
00:21:41.801 --> 00:21:44.470
[cannons boom]

420
00:21:44.470 --> 00:21:46.764
- [Dr. Lieb] Having Soviet boots
on German ground

421
00:21:46.764 --> 00:21:50.392
is a major blow for
the German psyche

422
00:21:50.392 --> 00:21:55.397
because they consider the
Soviets as their mortal enemies.

423
00:21:56.148 --> 00:21:58.567
and this is a disaster for them.

424
00:21:58.567 --> 00:22:00.361
- [Sean] The war is finally
being brought home

425
00:22:00.361 --> 00:22:02.363
to the Germans.

426
00:22:03.697 --> 00:22:06.075
- [Dr. Lieb] In theory. the
Nazi authorities

427
00:22:06.075 --> 00:22:08.786
would've had the
time for months

428
00:22:08.786 --> 00:22:11.121
to evacuate
the civilians.

429
00:22:11.121 --> 00:22:13.249
but that's something
they didn't do.

430
00:22:13.249 --> 00:22:15.709
because if you stay
there. you'll show that

431
00:22:15.709 --> 00:22:17.086
you've got more confidence

432
00:22:17.211 --> 00:22:19.255
and that you are defending
your home territory.

433
00:22:21.298 --> 00:22:23.384
- [Geoffrey] But basically.
the Russians come

434
00:22:23.384 --> 00:22:24.802
with such overwhelming force

435
00:22:24.802 --> 00:22:26.637
that the Germans can't
stop them at the border.

436
00:22:26.637 --> 00:22:29.765
And so this causes mass
panic as the German civilians

437
00:22:29.765 --> 00:22:32.685
take to the roads to try to
escape this Russian onslaught.

438
00:22:32.685 --> 00:22:35.563
knowing full well what
awaits if they stay.

439
00:22:35.563 --> 00:22:37.648
[cannon booms]

440
00:22:37.648 --> 00:22:40.442
- [Sean] The Germans have
fought a horrific war

441
00:22:40.442 --> 00:22:43.028
of annihilation in
the Soviet Union.

442
00:22:45.447 --> 00:22:47.491
Now the Soviets are finally able

443
00:22:47.491 --> 00:22:49.869
to take revenge
against the Germans.

444
00:22:54.582 --> 00:22:57.167
- [Geoffrey] They looted and
they pillaged and they raped

445
00:22:57.167 --> 00:22:59.044
and they burned
and they destroyed.

446
00:22:59.044 --> 00:23:00.796
and they took pleasure
in doing these things

447
00:23:00.796 --> 00:23:02.631
as they advanced.

448
00:23:02.631 --> 00:23:05.134
[somber music]

449
00:23:07.177 --> 00:23:11.265
- [Sean] There's 100.000 or more
deaths on the German side.

450
00:23:11.265 --> 00:23:12.975
and something like maybe a fifth

451
00:23:12.975 --> 00:23:15.227
of the female
population is raped.

452
00:23:19.189 --> 00:23:23.611
- This is the beginning of
what the Germans can expect

453
00:23:23.611 --> 00:23:26.655
to receive when Red
Army break into Berlin.

454
00:23:32.244 --> 00:23:34.121
- [Tom] Joseph Stalin engineers

455
00:23:34.121 --> 00:23:37.374
the Soviet Union's final moves.

456
00:23:37.374 --> 00:23:40.836
as the Red Army continues its
march west

457
00:23:41.921 --> 00:23:43.756
towards Berlin.

458
00:23:43.756 --> 00:23:47.051
- [Sean] Berlin is really the be
all. end all of the war.

459
00:23:47.051 --> 00:23:49.178
This is where we have
the Reich Chancellery.

460
00:23:49.178 --> 00:23:51.305
where we have the
Reichstag building.

461
00:23:51.305 --> 00:23:53.390
where Hitler has his bunker.

462
00:23:53.390 --> 00:23:56.435
Once the Red Army reaches
Berlin. the war will be over

463
00:23:56.435 --> 00:23:58.938
and it will be a great
victory and a great triumph.

464
00:23:58.938 --> 00:24:00.481
[crowd speaks in
foreign language]

465
00:24:00.481 --> 00:24:02.191
- [Col. Douds] For someone who
lives in Berlin.

466
00:24:02.191 --> 00:24:05.486
It's not lost on them what
happens in East Prussia.

467
00:24:05.486 --> 00:24:07.363
The Soviets are
getting retribution

468
00:24:07.363 --> 00:24:10.616
and it's coming in the
form of German bodies.

469
00:24:10.616 --> 00:24:14.495
German blood. rapes. killings.
and that's coming your way.

470
00:24:15.579 --> 00:24:19.291
Almost the image of an incoming
tide that you cannot stop.

471
00:24:19.291 --> 00:24:20.250
[bomb booms]

472
00:24:23.337 --> 00:24:24.338
[tense music]

473
00:24:30.344 --> 00:24:31.804
- [Tom] In the spring of 1945.

474
00:24:31.929 --> 00:24:34.723
Germany is under assault
from multiple directions.

475
00:24:34.723 --> 00:24:36.350
[cannon booms]

476
00:24:38.644 --> 00:24:43.816
In the east. the Red Army
rapidly advances towards Berlin.

477
00:24:43.816 --> 00:24:46.652
In the west. the allies
continue on a broad front

478
00:24:46.652 --> 00:24:48.654
as they approach
the Rhine River.

479
00:24:52.491 --> 00:24:55.202
- [Paul] The Rhine is the
German's last

480
00:24:55.202 --> 00:24:57.121
key strategic position

481
00:24:57.121 --> 00:24:59.123
to try and delay the inevitable

482
00:24:59.123 --> 00:25:01.083
of the allies
getting into Germany

483
00:25:01.083 --> 00:25:02.793
and defeating the Third Reich.

484
00:25:03.252 --> 00:25:06.880
- [Geoffrey] It's a big. broad
river. fast-flowing. deep.

485
00:25:06.880 --> 00:25:08.841
and the Germans know
this. so they're planning

486
00:25:08.841 --> 00:25:11.510
to kind of defend
every inch of it.

487
00:25:12.469 --> 00:25:14.513
- [Dr. Lieb] Their defense
strategy in the west is

488
00:25:14.513 --> 00:25:17.641
to blow up all the bridges
across the River Rhine.

489
00:25:19.643 --> 00:25:21.937
To use this huge
natural barrier.

490
00:25:26.483 --> 00:25:28.610
- [Tom] British Field
Marshal Bernard Montgomery

491
00:25:28.610 --> 00:25:31.613
designs an operation that
will take Allied Forces

492
00:25:31.613 --> 00:25:34.366
across the Rhine and
further into Germany.

493
00:25:36.076 --> 00:25:39.329
But unexpectedly. the
American 9th Armored Division

494
00:25:39.329 --> 00:25:42.041
discovers another way
into the German Reich.

495
00:25:46.170 --> 00:25:48.589
- [Paul] Really. out of
nowhere. an advanced unit

496
00:25:48.589 --> 00:25:51.592
of Americans ends up
at the Remagen Bridge.

497
00:25:51.592 --> 00:25:53.427
the key bridge across the Rhine.

498
00:25:53.427 --> 00:25:56.722
And the Germans. they failed
to destroy the bridge properly.

499
00:25:58.891 --> 00:26:00.642
- [Martin] That's not because
the Germans were dumb.

500
00:26:00.642 --> 00:26:02.102
the Germans tried
to blow the bridge.

501
00:26:02.102 --> 00:26:03.103
It's just that they didn't have

502
00:26:03.103 --> 00:26:04.813
enough explosives to do the job.

503
00:26:05.647 --> 00:26:06.857
- [Geoffrey] But it was very
stoutly built.

504
00:26:06.857 --> 00:26:08.400
The bridge just kind
of jumps on these

505
00:26:08.400 --> 00:26:09.818
really heavy stone piers

506
00:26:09.818 --> 00:26:11.653
and then settles back into
place.

507
00:26:13.947 --> 00:26:15.824
The Allies couldn't
believe their luck.

508
00:26:15.824 --> 00:26:18.327
so they raced forward
and they took the bridge.

509
00:26:18.327 --> 00:26:19.536
And they get across the Rhine

510
00:26:19.536 --> 00:26:21.330
three weeks earlier
than anticipated.

511
00:26:22.873 --> 00:26:25.584
- Once you're over the Rhine.
you're into Germany proper.

512
00:26:26.794 --> 00:26:29.004
It's a crucial moment
for the war in the West.

513
00:26:32.174 --> 00:26:35.552
- [Dr. Lieb] For the Germans.
this is a huge blow

514
00:26:35.552 --> 00:26:38.430
because now the
Allies can bring in

515
00:26:38.430 --> 00:26:39.807
reinforcements much quicker

516
00:26:39.807 --> 00:26:42.267
and Hitler is absolutely
furious about this.

517
00:26:43.102 --> 00:26:45.270
- [Robert] Oh. Hitler is prone
to rage at this time.

518
00:26:45.270 --> 00:26:47.356
and he demands that
everyone responsible

519
00:26:47.356 --> 00:26:49.483
will be immediately
court marshaled.

520
00:26:49.483 --> 00:26:52.027
not brought to
Berlin to explain.

521
00:26:52.027 --> 00:26:55.697
but a drumhead court marshal
in the field and shot.

522
00:26:55.697 --> 00:26:58.367
[somber music]

523
00:27:05.040 --> 00:27:06.708
- [Tom] Hitler
retreats to Berlin.

524
00:27:07.960 --> 00:27:11.922
He orders the destruction
of bridges. roads. railways.

525
00:27:11.922 --> 00:27:16.760
factories. anything that
can aid the allied advance.

526
00:27:18.971 --> 00:27:24.059
- [Martin] This Nero order named
in honor of the Roman Emperor.

527
00:27:24.059 --> 00:27:27.145
who famously allowed the
city of Rome to burn.

528
00:27:27.145 --> 00:27:29.231
would authorize German forces

529
00:27:29.231 --> 00:27:32.401
to destroy absolutely
everything as they retreated.

530
00:27:32.401 --> 00:27:33.819
[thunderous explosion]

531
00:27:33.819 --> 00:27:35.320
- [Dan] Blow up the bridges.
blow up the sanitation.

532
00:27:35.320 --> 00:27:36.780
blow up the power plants.

533
00:27:36.905 --> 00:27:39.700
even if it doesn't do any
good in the war effort.

534
00:27:39.700 --> 00:27:43.078
There's no reason to worry
about a post-war Germany.

535
00:27:44.997 --> 00:27:47.207
He stopped caring about
the individual people

536
00:27:47.207 --> 00:27:51.086
'cause they're no longer
worthy of surviving the war.

537
00:27:57.926 --> 00:27:59.636
- [Tom] Hitler
commands his loyal

538
00:27:59.636 --> 00:28:02.639
and capable minister of
armaments. Albert Speer.

539
00:28:02.639 --> 00:28:04.516
to carry out his order.

540
00:28:05.726 --> 00:28:07.185
Speer refuses.

541
00:28:08.478 --> 00:28:10.439
- [Geoffrey] Because he sees
that Hitler's. you know.

542
00:28:10.439 --> 00:28:11.940
gone mad essentially.

543
00:28:12.065 --> 00:28:13.442
And Speer actually comes to
Berlin and says. you know.

544
00:28:13.442 --> 00:28:17.154
right before the end. and he
says. "I haven't done it."

545
00:28:18.739 --> 00:28:21.199
- [Dr. Lieb] This shows that the
bond between Hitler

546
00:28:21.199 --> 00:28:24.536
and his leadership is being
broken to a certain degree.

547
00:28:26.038 --> 00:28:29.166
It's almost to the very last
days. the crumbling Third Reich

548
00:28:29.166 --> 00:28:32.878
that this link finally
starts to collapse.

549
00:28:32.878 --> 00:28:35.839
Hitler has now lost control
of the entire situation.

550
00:28:35.839 --> 00:28:38.133
He's now focused only
on the battle of Berlin.

551
00:28:39.176 --> 00:28:41.887
[somber music]

552
00:28:45.682 --> 00:28:48.810
- [Tom] In the garden outside
the Reich Chancellery.

553
00:28:48.810 --> 00:28:52.272
the Führer reviews a
formation of Hitler youth

554
00:28:52.272 --> 00:28:53.649
who have been awarded
the Knight's Cross

555
00:28:53.649 --> 00:28:55.150
for bravery in battle.

556
00:28:56.443 --> 00:28:59.529
Now. many will be
ordered to defend Berlin.

557
00:29:00.572 --> 00:29:04.493
- [Robert] The Hitler youth.
14 and 15 and 16-year-old boys.

558
00:29:04.493 --> 00:29:07.579
[youth speaks in
foreign language]

559
00:29:07.579 --> 00:29:11.041
- [Robert] By any analysis.
this is insane.

560
00:29:12.125 --> 00:29:13.961
- [Geoffrey] And he comes up
out of the bunker

561
00:29:13.961 --> 00:29:18.840
and he pins metals on these
sort of beardless little boys.

562
00:29:18.840 --> 00:29:21.843
Any rational onlooker can
see that Hitler has lost

563
00:29:21.843 --> 00:29:23.804
all attachment to reason.

564
00:29:25.764 --> 00:29:28.684
- [Robert] It may be he's
thinking of the last lost war.

565
00:29:29.685 --> 00:29:34.648
but I think 1918 is enough
of a obsession with Hitler

566
00:29:34.898 --> 00:29:36.525
that he is determined

567
00:29:36.525 --> 00:29:38.485
that Germany will not
give in this time.

568
00:29:38.485 --> 00:29:39.987
There will be no surrender.

569
00:29:39.987 --> 00:29:42.531
There will be total
war to the end.

570
00:29:42.531 --> 00:29:44.449
If Germany is gonna go down.

571
00:29:44.449 --> 00:29:47.160
it's going to go down
in a blaze of glory.

572
00:29:52.874 --> 00:29:53.875
[tense music]

573
00:29:56.962 --> 00:29:59.131
- [Tom] Allied forces
rapidly advanced

574
00:29:59.131 --> 00:30:03.176
through the Ruhr Valley and
into the heart of Germany.

575
00:30:03.176 --> 00:30:04.761
The British and
Americans had agreed

576
00:30:04.761 --> 00:30:07.431
that Soviet forces
should capture Berlin.

577
00:30:08.348 --> 00:30:11.643
but Stalin grows suspicious
of allied success.

578
00:30:14.021 --> 00:30:16.815
- [Michel] You have to remember
that Stalin is naturally

579
00:30:16.815 --> 00:30:20.402
and not unreasonably
deeply mistrustful.

580
00:30:20.402 --> 00:30:23.071
So when the Western
Allies start pouring

581
00:30:23.071 --> 00:30:26.199
into Western Germany far
faster than anyone expects.

582
00:30:26.199 --> 00:30:28.160
Stalin fears that
there may be something

583
00:30:28.160 --> 00:30:29.327
that he doesn't see.

584
00:30:30.537 --> 00:30:33.165
- [Simon] Stalin is always
paranoid

585
00:30:33.165 --> 00:30:36.543
that the Western powers
are going to make a deal

586
00:30:36.543 --> 00:30:39.129
with the Germans
at the last minute

587
00:30:39.129 --> 00:30:41.673
against the Soviet Union.
against the Communists.

588
00:30:52.267 --> 00:30:55.729
- [Tom] In Moscow. Stalin
summons Marshal Georgy Zhukov.

589
00:30:55.729 --> 00:30:59.232
the hero of
Stalingrad and Kursk.

590
00:30:59.232 --> 00:31:00.901
and Marshal Ivan Konev.

591
00:31:00.901 --> 00:31:03.153
who has led the first
Ukrainian front.

592
00:31:03.153 --> 00:31:05.697
a famed Red Army group
throughout the war.

593
00:31:09.659 --> 00:31:12.454
- [Simon] He sits there with
the map and he says.

594
00:31:12.454 --> 00:31:14.206
"Who's gonna take Berlin?"

595
00:31:15.165 --> 00:31:17.417
- [Sean] So Stalin effectively
sets up

596
00:31:17.417 --> 00:31:19.211
a kind of race between them

597
00:31:19.836 --> 00:31:22.172
to see who will
take Berlin first.

598
00:31:22.172 --> 00:31:24.716
So this is a way of
motivating his generals

599
00:31:24.716 --> 00:31:27.636
because Stalin. of
course. wanted to ensure

600
00:31:27.636 --> 00:31:30.806
that the Red Army would be
the first to reach Berlin.

601
00:31:30.806 --> 00:31:34.893
- [Simon] And in an amazing
scene. both Marshals salute

602
00:31:34.893 --> 00:31:38.146
and leave the room
and run to their cars

603
00:31:38.146 --> 00:31:40.482
to start the race to Berlin.

604
00:31:41.525 --> 00:31:44.194
[tense music]

605
00:31:46.947 --> 00:31:50.242
- [Tom] By mid-April. the Red
Army is closing in on Berlin.

606
00:31:51.952 --> 00:31:54.162
Zhukov's forces
approach from the east.

607
00:31:55.288 --> 00:31:57.666
Konev's troops will
attack from the south.

608
00:31:59.000 --> 00:32:01.086
- [Sean] The final assault
on Berlin begins

609
00:32:01.086 --> 00:32:03.922
with a ferocious
artillery barrage.

610
00:32:03.922 --> 00:32:05.757
[cannon booms]

611
00:32:05.757 --> 00:32:08.385
[cannons boom]

612
00:32:12.639 --> 00:32:17.561
Something like 9.000 guns
rained down 1.2 million shells.

613
00:32:18.145 --> 00:32:20.397
[cannons hiss]

614
00:32:21.648 --> 00:32:23.817
- [Geoffrey] To put that in
context. the British fired

615
00:32:23.817 --> 00:32:25.485
one million rounds of artillery

616
00:32:25.485 --> 00:32:27.279
onto the German
trenches on the Somme

617
00:32:27.279 --> 00:32:29.030
over like two weeks
in World War I.

618
00:32:30.490 --> 00:32:34.452
Now. in one day more shells
into the streets of Berlin.

619
00:32:38.874 --> 00:32:40.250
- [Tom] Zhukov's forces meet

620
00:32:40.375 --> 00:32:44.212
particularly fierce resistance
in the Seelow heights.

621
00:32:44.212 --> 00:32:47.799
an area the Germans consider
the gates of Berlin.

622
00:32:50.135 --> 00:32:52.095
- [Sean] The Germans are dug in.

623
00:32:52.095 --> 00:32:53.847
They have no desire to surrender

624
00:32:53.847 --> 00:32:56.433
because they know they
would be viewed as traitors.

625
00:32:57.350 --> 00:33:01.229
Berlin is meant to be a
fortress city. Festung Berlin.

626
00:33:01.229 --> 00:33:03.523
This means it has to be
defended at all costs.

627
00:33:05.817 --> 00:33:08.278
- [Paul] Hitler's order
was to keep fighting

628
00:33:08.278 --> 00:33:10.280
until there's nothing left.

629
00:33:10.280 --> 00:33:13.158
They're not gonna admit
the war's been lost.

630
00:33:13.158 --> 00:33:15.994
- [Dr. Lieb] Hitler is now
facing total defeat.

631
00:33:15.994 --> 00:33:18.872
and he wants to drag
the entire German people

632
00:33:18.872 --> 00:33:20.957
into this total defeat.

633
00:33:22.167 --> 00:33:24.169
- [Dan] The population has been
pressed into service.

634
00:33:24.169 --> 00:33:26.630
They've been. you know.
building tank traps

635
00:33:26.630 --> 00:33:27.881
and digging ditches.

636
00:33:28.798 --> 00:33:31.218
But I don't think you can
fool a bunch of people

637
00:33:31.218 --> 00:33:33.345
who are living in
cities that are rubble.

638
00:33:33.345 --> 00:33:35.972
You hear the artillery
in the distance

639
00:33:35.972 --> 00:33:38.350
that the Soviets are
shooting at your city.

640
00:33:38.350 --> 00:33:40.393
I mean. we're past
the time of illusions.

641
00:33:40.393 --> 00:33:42.354
You're people at
the end of the rope.

642
00:33:43.521 --> 00:33:45.106
- [Geoffrey] The German troops
that are left.

643
00:33:45.106 --> 00:33:48.693
it's this bizarre
assembly of overage people

644
00:33:48.693 --> 00:33:51.363
that normally wouldn't
be drafted or underage.

645
00:33:53.323 --> 00:33:56.993
- [Martin] You have a large
number of very young members

646
00:33:56.993 --> 00:33:58.203
of the Volkssturm.

647
00:33:59.704 --> 00:34:02.040
They were divided into
these tank hunting units

648
00:34:02.040 --> 00:34:04.167
where they were 12
and 13-year-old boys

649
00:34:04.167 --> 00:34:05.335
that were equipped with this

650
00:34:05.460 --> 00:34:07.087
very effective
German anti-tank weapon

651
00:34:07.087 --> 00:34:08.295
called the Panzerfaust.

652
00:34:10.340 --> 00:34:12.759
- [Geoffrey] These basically
one-shot German bazookas.

653
00:34:12.759 --> 00:34:14.844
and they're gonna be in
these load of fighting holes

654
00:34:14.844 --> 00:34:18.139
waiting for the Soviet tanks
to come and take their one shot

655
00:34:18.139 --> 00:34:21.226
and then be. you know. crushed
into pulp under the treads.

656
00:34:22.893 --> 00:34:25.313
- [Paul] The ideology of the
Reich has gone out the window.

657
00:34:25.313 --> 00:34:27.607
You don't know what you're
fighting for anymore.

658
00:34:29.275 --> 00:34:32.279
You are now protecting your
street and your friends

659
00:34:32.279 --> 00:34:34.906
and your family from the
marauders that are coming.

660
00:34:36.908 --> 00:34:41.036
- [Geoffrey] If you're still in
Berlin by April 1945.

661
00:34:41.036 --> 00:34:42.080
you're not gonna get out.

662
00:34:43.248 --> 00:34:45.625
So you're fighting
for your life.

663
00:34:45.625 --> 00:34:47.668
[bazooka booms]

664
00:34:50.755 --> 00:34:51.880
[tense music]

665
00:34:59.848 --> 00:35:03.018
- [Tom] On April
19th. Zhukov's troops

666
00:35:03.018 --> 00:35:06.313
break through the German
lines at Seelow Heights.

667
00:35:06.313 --> 00:35:09.441
Konev enters the Nazi
capital from the south.

668
00:35:11.318 --> 00:35:13.612
[guns bang]

669
00:35:16.948 --> 00:35:18.867
- [Simon] Battle of Berlin is
brutal.

670
00:35:20.160 --> 00:35:21.828
[guns bang]

671
00:35:21.828 --> 00:35:23.955
It's an urban battlefield.

672
00:35:23.955 --> 00:35:27.208
which is the hardest sort of
fighting and the most costly.

673
00:35:27.208 --> 00:35:29.336
[guns bang]

674
00:35:29.336 --> 00:35:31.588
It's impossible not to
take every building.

675
00:35:31.588 --> 00:35:33.214
You can't leave
buildings behind you.

676
00:35:33.381 --> 00:35:36.343
You're under fire all the time
from buildings on both sides.

677
00:35:38.386 --> 00:35:40.138
Large amounts of
civilians are killed.

678
00:35:40.138 --> 00:35:43.808
and it's incredibly
slow and dangerous.

679
00:35:43.808 --> 00:35:46.394
[tense music]

680
00:35:48.146 --> 00:35:50.649
- [Geoffrey] This moonscape of
Berlin that's already been

681
00:35:50.649 --> 00:35:54.277
just shattered to rubble
is now just being pounded

682
00:35:54.277 --> 00:35:55.862
by companies of Soviet infantry

683
00:35:55.862 --> 00:35:57.989
filtering into the
city from all points.

684
00:35:57.989 --> 00:35:59.991
I mean. literally all points.

685
00:35:59.991 --> 00:36:02.452
[tense music]

686
00:36:11.252 --> 00:36:15.340
- [Simon] But in the end. this
extraordinary battle.

687
00:36:15.340 --> 00:36:20.428
the Soviet troops begin to
converge on the Chancellery.

688
00:36:20.887 --> 00:36:23.390
[tense music]

689
00:36:24.724 --> 00:36:27.227
- [Tom] Beneath the
Reich Chancellery.

690
00:36:27.227 --> 00:36:29.187
Hitler is sequestered
in a bunker

691
00:36:29.187 --> 00:36:31.690
with his companion. Eva Braun.

692
00:36:31.690 --> 00:36:34.401
and surrounded by
aides. secretaries.

693
00:36:34.401 --> 00:36:36.194
and Nazi party officials.

694
00:36:37.487 --> 00:36:39.989
He believes that the military

695
00:36:39.989 --> 00:36:43.618
and the German people
have let him down.

696
00:36:43.618 --> 00:36:46.037
- [Sean] Hitler wants to keep
the resistance going

697
00:36:46.037 --> 00:36:47.831
for as long as
possible to inflict

698
00:36:47.831 --> 00:36:50.458
as much damage on
the invading armies.

699
00:36:50.458 --> 00:36:55.130
However. he does not want to
outlast. to outlive the war.

700
00:36:55.130 --> 00:36:57.716
He does not want to
become a prisoner of war.

701
00:36:57.716 --> 00:37:00.385
He does not want to become
some type of curiosity

702
00:37:00.385 --> 00:37:02.470
exhibited by his enemies.

703
00:37:03.763 --> 00:37:08.059
- [Robert] And so he has to stay
alive as long as possible.

704
00:37:08.059 --> 00:37:10.687
as close to the
bitter end as possible

705
00:37:10.687 --> 00:37:15.066
so that there will never really
be an idea of Nazi Germany

706
00:37:15.066 --> 00:37:18.111
in people's minds that does
not include Adolf Hitler.

707
00:37:19.279 --> 00:37:23.324
He's going to go down
in Wagnerian fashion

708
00:37:23.324 --> 00:37:24.909
and take a world with him.

709
00:37:25.952 --> 00:37:28.496
[tense music]

710
00:37:34.586 --> 00:37:36.880
- [Tom] On April 29th.
Hitler is informed

711
00:37:36.880 --> 00:37:40.008
that his longtime ally.
the Italian dictator

712
00:37:40.008 --> 00:37:43.803
Benito Mussolini.
has been executed.

713
00:37:43.803 --> 00:37:47.265
His body put on display
by Italian partisans.

714
00:37:48.933 --> 00:37:51.561
- [Geoffrey] Mussolini has just
been hung upside down

715
00:37:51.561 --> 00:37:53.897
in a gas station in
northern Italy.

716
00:37:53.897 --> 00:37:55.648
along with his mistress.
Clara Petacci.

717
00:37:55.648 --> 00:37:59.277
where he's like mocked and
spat upon and vilified.

718
00:38:02.030 --> 00:38:03.990
Hitler fears the same
fate for himself.

719
00:38:05.617 --> 00:38:08.203
- The Soviets are right
outside the Führer bunker.

720
00:38:08.203 --> 00:38:10.830
He's listening to the
shelling happening above him.

721
00:38:14.959 --> 00:38:18.755
- [Martin] And so Adolf Hitler.
on April 30th. 1945.

722
00:38:18.755 --> 00:38:22.550
commits suicide in the Führer
bunker along with Eva Braun

723
00:38:25.845 --> 00:38:28.056
in a city that has
been reduced to rubble.

724
00:38:29.641 --> 00:38:32.393
[somber music]

725
00:38:38.566 --> 00:38:40.109
- [Simon] When Hitler commits
suicide.

726
00:38:40.109 --> 00:38:43.363
Stalin is woken in the
night by Marshal Zhukov.

727
00:38:43.363 --> 00:38:45.448
and Marshal Zhukov says to him.

728
00:38:45.448 --> 00:38:47.534
"Marshal Stalin. I've got news.

729
00:38:47.534 --> 00:38:49.911
Hitler is dead and he's
committed suicide in the ruins."

730
00:38:49.911 --> 00:38:51.162
and there's a long silence.

731
00:38:51.162 --> 00:38:53.289
And then Stalin
says something like.

732
00:38:53.289 --> 00:38:55.041
"So that's the end
of the bastard."

733
00:38:55.041 --> 00:38:58.002
Puts the phone down
and goes back to sleep.

734
00:38:58.127 --> 00:39:00.839
[somber music]

735
00:39:12.976 --> 00:39:16.271
- [Tom] On May 2nd. the
Soviets raised their flag

736
00:39:16.271 --> 00:39:18.106
above the ruins
of the Reichstag.

737
00:39:21.734 --> 00:39:24.946
On May 7th. German
General Alfred Jodl

738
00:39:24.946 --> 00:39:28.449
surrenders to the Western
Allies at Reims. France.

739
00:39:30.368 --> 00:39:33.496
A day later. the Germans
officially surrendered

740
00:39:33.496 --> 00:39:34.706
to the Soviets.

741
00:39:35.415 --> 00:39:36.791
- With the stroke of the pen.

742
00:39:36.791 --> 00:39:41.129
Nazi Germany ceases to
exist on May 8th. 1945.

743
00:39:41.129 --> 00:39:43.756
[tense music]

744
00:39:48.845 --> 00:39:51.806
- [Harry] This is a solemn
but a glorious hour.

745
00:39:52.891 --> 00:39:56.728
General Eisenhower informs
me that the forces of Germany

746
00:39:56.728 --> 00:39:58.855
has surrendered to
the United Nations.

747
00:40:00.231 --> 00:40:02.400
- [Michel] Here we are at the
end of a brutal war

748
00:40:02.400 --> 00:40:05.361
against a brutal
adversary in Europe.

749
00:40:05.361 --> 00:40:09.407
And there was such great
costs with so much exhaustion.

750
00:40:09.407 --> 00:40:11.409
It's almost
impossible to imagine

751
00:40:11.409 --> 00:40:12.952
what that must have been like.

752
00:40:17.373 --> 00:40:20.209
- [Harry] Our rejoicing
is sobered and subdued

753
00:40:20.335 --> 00:40:23.838
by a supreme consciousness
of the terrible price

754
00:40:23.838 --> 00:40:27.133
we have paid to rid
the world of Hitler

755
00:40:27.133 --> 00:40:29.135
and his evil band.

756
00:40:30.803 --> 00:40:33.514
- [Simon] Hitler was the
ultimate reckless gambler.

757
00:40:34.682 --> 00:40:37.936
Risking everything. even
Germany. even Europe.

758
00:40:40.897 --> 00:40:43.274
- [Harry] Let us not
forget the sorrow

759
00:40:43.274 --> 00:40:46.402
and the heartache.
which today abide

760
00:40:46.402 --> 00:40:49.280
in the homes of so
many of our neighbors.

761
00:40:50.406 --> 00:40:52.283
- [Sean] The Second World
War. unlike the first.

762
00:40:52.283 --> 00:40:54.661
is one in which the
majority of the casualties

763
00:40:54.661 --> 00:40:57.372
actually happened among
the civilian population.

764
00:40:58.331 --> 00:41:00.041
A lot of it was
simply because of

765
00:41:00.041 --> 00:41:02.794
the vast atrocities committed.

766
00:41:02.794 --> 00:41:05.463
[somber music]

767
00:41:07.256 --> 00:41:11.636
The war left terrible scars
on the landscape of Europe

768
00:41:11.636 --> 00:41:13.930
and in the memories
of the populations.

769
00:41:17.225 --> 00:41:19.394
- [Harry] We must work
to bind up the wounds

770
00:41:19.394 --> 00:41:21.145
of a suffering world.

771
00:41:21.145 --> 00:41:25.316
The West is free. but the
East is still in bondage.

772
00:41:26.567 --> 00:41:31.364
- In the popular mind. World
War II tends to wrap up

773
00:41:31.364 --> 00:41:33.574
with the glory of VE Day.

774
00:41:35.368 --> 00:41:37.620
It did not happen that way

775
00:41:37.620 --> 00:41:40.415
for the people who
were fighting it.

776
00:41:41.708 --> 00:41:45.003
In the Pacific. there's
no end in sight.

777
00:41:46.254 --> 00:41:48.631
- [Harry] When the
last Japanese division

778
00:41:48.631 --> 00:41:51.801
has surrendered unconditionally.

779
00:41:51.801 --> 00:41:54.846
then only will our
fighting job be done.

780
00:41:56.097 --> 00:42:00.601
Until that day. let no
man abandon his post

781
00:42:00.601 --> 00:42:01.978
or slacken his efforts.

782
00:42:04.313 --> 00:42:06.399
[plane zooms]

783
00:42:06.399 --> 00:42:11.446
- After VE Day. Europeans
facing chaos and uncertainty

784
00:42:11.446 --> 00:42:13.114
begin the long work of putting

785
00:42:13.114 --> 00:42:15.283
their shattered
world back together.

786
00:42:16.117 --> 00:42:19.787
In the Pacific. the war
is reaching a crescendo.

787
00:42:19.787 --> 00:42:21.456
As the United States
fights its way

788
00:42:21.456 --> 00:42:23.249
to the Japanese home islands.

789
00:42:23.249 --> 00:42:27.253
a new weapon is tested in
the deserts of New Mexico.

790
00:42:27.253 --> 00:42:31.758
A noiseless flash with a
potential to change the world.

790
